I bought a 3D printer during the first wave of Covid, initally to 3D print face shields for frontline workers. Since I was at home and had a lot of time on my hand and not a lot to do, I quickly got wayy too much into 3D printing, and designing.



This is just a dump of some images, with some description:

PyCon India 2020 went online, and everyone knows the best part of a FOSS conference is the swags xD, so naturally  I designed a small keychain based off the logo in Fusion 360. I did not have red and gold fillament so I requested a friend Kristoff Braganza to print it for me. He is also an amazing photographer I got some cool photos of the final result:


![3DprinitingRoll18](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll18.jpg)
![3DprinitingRoll24](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll24.jpg)
![3DprinitingRoll25](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll25.jpg)

A little Baby Yoda, this was an open source model from Thingiverse, one of my first 3D prints. I sanded it down, filled it with some car/mechanical filler, and gave it a paint job using some acrylic colors:

![3DprinitingRoll36](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll36.jpg)

Behold, Tormund Giantsbane:
