A Rick and Morty keychain formy friend Aayush's birthday:
![3DprinitingRoll29](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll29.jpg)

A penrose triangle coaster, one of the the first attempts with changing color midway during a print, and also playing with exposing infill patterns. The centre piece is a gyroid infill pattern which is exposed and printed in a translucent PLA so the light can shine from behind. I am surpriced what one can do on a single nozzle printer and some gcode edits. 
![3DprinitingRoll31](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll31.jpg)

Designed and printed some coasters for my friends company, playing with exposing infill patterns:
![3DprinitingRoll32](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll32.jpg)


A voronoi klien bottle
![3DprinitingRoll33](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll33.jpg)

This was actually quite fun and a bit challenging, i used fusion 360 to design a custom case for an Arduino Uni. The Arduino Uno was not according to specifications haha so I did a lot of manual measurements and testing and making again :
![3DprinitingRoll34](/images/3Dprinting/3dprintingRoll34.jpg)

A part of the GOT coaster series, this one is for House targaryen:
